# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Two reasons, and both matter. Size: the visual pack, the masterplan and every
# `node_modules` in the workspace are hundreds of megabytes that would be sent
# to the daemon on every build. Correctness: a `node_modules` built on the host
# is the wrong platform's binaries, and a stale `dist` copied in is a build that
# silently ships yesterday's code.

.git
.github
.githooks

# Installed and built on the host. Both are produced inside the image instead.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Source material and working files, none of which any build reads.
01_Masterplan
02_Claude_Guides
03_Visual_Pack
_archive
assets
simulations
tools/art/out

# Secrets never reach a build context, whatever else happens.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Foundry output; the contracts are built by their own toolchain.
out
cache
broadcast
